WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:04.780
<i>I'm Hasegawa Kouta. 17 year
old high school second-year.</i>

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.210
<i>The five of us went to Puroland
like we've always dreamed!</i>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.500
<i>It was so much fun and the best ever!</i>

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>It really was a dream come true.</i>

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>That's where I found it.</i>

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.530
Okay!

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.560
I want to be like them!

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.050
I want to be like Purin, Kitty, My
Melody, Cinnamoroll, and Kiki and Lala!

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.370
And... like all of you.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.510
I want to sparkle, too!

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.950
Sparkle?

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.760
Not Kiki and Lala?

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.100
So, what do you want to do?

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:46.900
Right!

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.500
That's...

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.440
That's...?

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.150
I'm not sure.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:37.090
Sparkling Rhapsody

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.330
Well, I guess we kind of get
that you want to do something.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.440
But you don't know the
important details, do you?

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.730
Sorry.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.740
Why don't you try really thinking
about the sparkling again?

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.640
I want to sparkle,

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.750
but what do I want to do?

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.820
You're really agonizing over this, aren't you?

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:18.500
Guess I better give you some advice then.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.550
I mean,

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.580
I am your number one friend after all!

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:23.300
No, you're just his classmate.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.390
What, you're still fretting over that?

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.230
Hey, Hase!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.790
Yeah,

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.390
Hey, where's Shunsuke?

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:30.180
I'm right here, wait!

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.180
He had some team stuff during lunch break.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.290
The soccer team has it rough.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:32.190
I'm right here!

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.420
I see...

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.950
Why don't you try really thinking
about the sparkling again?

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.290
That's it!

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:51.190
Yuu, thanks! I knew you'd help me out!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.810
I don't really get what's
going on, but good luck.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:54.610
Yeah.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.590
You okay?

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.250
I don't really know.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.620
Well, you weren't actually
dumped by Hase just now.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.030
You just never existed for him to begin with.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.100
Which means, Hasegawa
is joining the team as a trial.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.810
Please take care of me.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.610
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.400
What are you doing?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.430
Did you find your sparkle?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.630
I came here to find it.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.360
Huh?

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:30.530
<i>The source of sparkling for me is
Yuu and Shunsuke and the others.</i>

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.460
<i>So if I'm with them, I might be
able to understand it more.</i>

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.640
Now then, let's start practice.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:39.960
Okay!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.270
That's enough of afternoon practice.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.770
G-Good job everyone.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.410
You okay?

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.380
I'm fine.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.900
<i>This isn't it.</i>

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.740
<b>Library</b>

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.230
You don't really need to help me.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:15.980
I want to.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.370
<i>I'll find it this time for sure!</i>

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.120
The book is due back after a week.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.910
Hey, please don't sleep here.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.260
I'm not sleeping, I'm not sleeping!

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.600
Please be careful.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.550
Jeez.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.860
I told you not to fall asleep!

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.370
Whoa.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.330
Do you want to try holding it?

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:52.870
Sure!

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.580
My feet fell asleep.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.500
Sorry for making you help me.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.510
No worries. I wanted to try cooking for once.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.690
Ow!

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.260
Hey, you okay?!

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.560
You are making something I can eat, right?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:28.450
Hey, Purin, there wasn't
anything for me to sparkle at.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.850
This is serious.

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.280
Totally serious.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.920
So hopeless...

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.020
Kouta-kun, are you okay?

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.400
What is it, Yuu?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.500
I'm not Yuu, I'm Melody-chan.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.340
So, you still can't find your sparkle?

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:48.590
No.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.010
That's tough.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.850
Right, Kitty?

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.060
I'm Kitty-san.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.220
Wh-What are they doing?

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.630
Hey, Senpai...

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:09.700
I'll think about it with you,
so hang in there, Kouta-kun.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.900
Not you, too, Senpai.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.810
Come on, Kiki and Lala should join us, too.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:15.620
Wha?!

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.260
We're Kiki and Lala.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.670
Do their voices properly.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:22.820
Senpai!

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.780
Hey, Kouta-kun. Why do you
feel that you want to sparkle?

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.030
That's because...

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:44.050
When I met you and Shunsuke and
you said you were the Sanrio Boys,

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:46.500
I was embarrassed but happy.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.360
And then I got to know President and Ryo.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.130
Everyone has something that
they devote themselves to.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.660
I thought how amazing and nice that must be.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.100
I vaguely felt like I wanted
to do something, too.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:06.610
But I could never figure
out what that thing was.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:14.660
The Miracle Gift Parade...

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:23.810
When I saw the Miracle Gift Parade,
I realized I wanted to sparkle.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.820
Then let's do it, the Miracle Gift Parade.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:37.700
Huh?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.490
We can sing and dance and put on a show.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.700
Sing and dance?

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.690
And put on a show?

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:47.420
In other words, a musical?

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:49.960
A musical?

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:51.710
It's a great idea!

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.510
Sounds interesting.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.180
Where would we do it though?

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.840
There's the school festival
in the second semester.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.550
That's perfect Shushu,

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:01.720
and, if I recall correctly, students can
participate in it individually, right?

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:03.870
W-Wait a minute!

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:07.610
I mean, are you sure?
We just decided that so easily.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.570
It sounds like a lot of fun though, right?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:10.700
Yeah.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.300
I don't think we can do it.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.860
What? Why?

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.780
That's true.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:23.190
There's so much to prepare
with the script, the music,

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:27.920
the costumes and the sets,
the props and rehearsals.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:30.250
Do you think amateurs
like us could do all that?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.310
You have a point.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:36.880
We can manage it with effort,
guts, and a positive attitude!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.120
Shunsuke, don't you have team activities?

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.690
I'll do my best for Shunsuke's portion.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:43.980
You can't, you have your
sister to think about, Yuu.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.800
Well, we can make it work somehow.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:46.880
But...

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.550
It's pointless to try and stop me now.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:53.200
I'm curious about your sparkle, too.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.130
Yuu...

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.250
Yeah,

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.320
let's make it Kittyful.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:04.220
Seriously, Shunsuke, what is "Kittyful"?

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.200
It just means Shushu's excited, too, right?

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.240
We will need to be prepared
if we're going to do this.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:11.460
It's not going to be a smooth ride.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.260
What do you want to do, Kouta?

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:20.650
I want to do it.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:22.970
I want to try doing it!

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:27.540
Understood.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.630
Let me join you, too.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:30.730
You, too, Senpai?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.480
So, what are <i>you</i> going to do, Ryo-chan?

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.730
Th-There's no way...

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:36.890
Ryo.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.900
Fine, I'll help, too.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.200
Thank you!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.700
Let's all do our best together!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.390
Please let go of me.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:55.420
Now then, if we're going to put
on a musical, there's one problem.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.390
Yes, the script.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.720
There is that.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.230
It's the music, right?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.360
That's another one.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.160
Costumes.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:03.180
That, too.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.310
It sounds like we have nothing
but problems when you say that.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.210
We have a much larger problem.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.170
That is...

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:13.190
Money.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.070
The heck, you meant money?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.120
Senpai, please don't scare me like that.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.130
Money is kind of... yeah.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:30.130
If we do a musical at the school festival,

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:33.750
it will be treated as an individual
student participation.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.650
In that instance, we would not
receive a budget from the school

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.690
like the classes or clubs do.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.020
It would all be out of pocket.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.990
If we estimate the cost of the musical

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:47.560
based on plays performed
at previous school festivals...

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:50.470
It adds up to about this much.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.060
No way!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:53.270
That much?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.520
That's absolutely hopeless with my allowance.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.160
Is this for real? Is that really the cost?

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.980
It's all right, I have an idea.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:01.900
You do?!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:02.700
Yes.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:10.660
<b>Job Information Magazine</b>

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:09.480
Securing the budget will be our
challenge for summer break.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:18.870
So we're stuck having to
work this summer break.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.420
I feel bad, this is all because of me...

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.570
What're you saying that for?

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:28.190
But you can't get a part-time job without
permission from someone at home, right?

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:29.740
Will you be okay?

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:33.580
I'll be fine. I'll just have to
have a hard talk with Yuri.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:34.510
Really?

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.440
I am her big brother after all.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.570
I'm really sorry!

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.570
I have to get a job for summer break.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:46.000
There might be days where I won't
be able to make your meals.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.700
What's that about? You get
a girlfriend or something?

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:50.480
Why do you ask?

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:56.900
Wh-Why? I figured it was to buy some
girlfriend a present or something.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.220
No, no, that's not it at all.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:01.720
I just have something I want to
do with Kouta and the others.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:05.590
O-Oh, is that all?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.750
So, can I?

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.190
Just do whatever.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.660
Thank you, Yuri!

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.100
A part-time job?

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:18.520
Yeah, it would only be during
summer break though,

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:19.530
is that okay?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.110
Why so sudden?

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.800
There's something I want to do with my friends
for the second semester school festival,

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:26.920
and I need money to do it.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.770
Is your allowance not going to be enough?

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.000
No, it won't be.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.120
Besides,

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:37.120
I want to try and do as much as I can myself.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.400
Kouta...

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:41.630
Go for it.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.250
You found something
you want to do, didn't you?

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:46.570
Yeah.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:52.030
<i>Once the first semester ended
and summer break started,</i>

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:55.230
<i>we began working right away.</i>

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.900
<i>I worked as a lifeguard at a pool.</i>

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:06.080
You there, please don't jump in the pool.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:08.990
Okay, let's go.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:10.310
Right.

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:13.990
<i>Shunsuke and President worked as movers.</i>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.000
Welcome.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.080
<i>Ryo was a waiter at a coffee shop.</i>

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.460
What will be having today?

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.130
Welcome.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.500
<i>And Yuu worked in fast food.</i>

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.490
This was how our summer break started.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:29.860
You're ordering Set A, correct?

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.180
Would you like a smile with that?

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.400
Huh, you would?

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.360
One smile coming right up.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.160
Here you go.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:52.490
Okay, gonna do my best today, too.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.690
Thank you very much.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:00.730
Waiter, more iced tea please!

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.420
Yes, right away.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.160
Are you ready for my order?

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:06.000
Yes, right away.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.150
Will you take my order, too?

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.970
Yes, one moment please.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:14.020
Nee-san, it's my turn with Ryo-chan right now.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:16.400
Don't intrude.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.370
Can I have a hot towel?

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.700
I said don't intrude.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.530
Are you going to order?
If not, please come take mine.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.150
Wait, I'm deciding now.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.950
Oh, what do you recommend, Ryo-chan?

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.110
Would you all knock it off!

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.910
And please sit together, it's a pain otherwise.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.410
Welcome.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.750
I'm here.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.410
Go home.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.700
Jumping is not allowed!

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:46.980
Shun?

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:48.710
Tomo-san.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.960
Part-time job, huh? That's rough.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:52.780
No, I'm doing fine.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.200
That so.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:55.470
Oh, right.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:56.770
Here.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.040
Make sure you make it to afternoon practice.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.230
Thanks!

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:13.990
It's okay, please don't cry.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.740
I'll find your mother right away, okay?

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:20.250
<b>2nd Practice Test</b>

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.250
Okay.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:24.980
I better hurry.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:29.750
Sorry I'm late, Yuri.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.760
I bought dinner at work.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.050
Oh, forgive the intrusion.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:37.520
Oh, hi.

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.810
I'm making dinner myself,
but if you bought something

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:41.680
you won't be having any then, right?

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.010
Ma-kun, wait just a bit longer.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.270
Yeah, okay.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:05.360
U-Um, Onii-sa—

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:08.740
You don't have the right to call me Onii-san!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.350
I'm sorry, please forgive me!

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.170
I'm home!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:17.500
Welcome back. Dinner is ready.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.680
I'll eat later.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:22.560
I hope Kouta's all right.
He's not eating either.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.610
Just let him do as he likes for now.

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:25.510
But...

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:26.770
He's fine.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:36.860
<b>Mizuno Yuu
Papa won't allow this.</b>

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:38.680
Papa?

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.200
<b>Papa won't allow this.</b>

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.370
<b>Papa won't allow this.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:47.170
<b>Papa won't allow this.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:51.800
<b>Nishimiya Ryo
How do you know?</b>

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:51.800
<b>Guys, come to my house at the end of the week.
I want to check on the budget.</b>

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.630
<b>Nishimiya Ryo
Got it, Senpai.</b>

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.140
It's huge!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.540
Yeah.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.410
Is this really the right place?

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:10.150
It's supposed to be...

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.660
Starting with rock. Rock,
paper, scissors, shoot!

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.110
After you then.

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:23.270
Good luck.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.910
We're counting on you, Senpai.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:27.410
I just gotta do it.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.140
What are you doing?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.440
This is your room?

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.050
Please don't stare so much, it's embarrassing.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.400
I-It's what?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.460
Let's look around!

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:57.260
Okay.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.490
Please stop.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.170
Hey, Kouta...

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:03.740
Are you going to keep wearing
those? You're being kind of rude.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:11.000
That's why I didn't want to take them off!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.000
Now then everyone, please enjoy.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:20.140
Are you a panda?

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:21.630
Mom...

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:28.860
Okay, looks like we'll be able
to secure the budget.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.770
Yay!

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:32.840
Which means our next concern is...

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.950
The content of the musical, right?

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.510
Yes, we need to decided
what we're going to do first,

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:41.240
then we'll have to prepare the
costumes, props, and music.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.790
Have you decided on what
you want the story to be?

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:47.400
Oh, well, I've been pretty busy with work.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:49.930
Hey now, get it together.

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.300
I know but...

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:54.290
He can't help it. A job alone keeps one busy.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:57.630
The things we need to prepare
will change based on the story,

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:00.020
so I think we should try to think about it.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:02.620
Nishimiya is right.

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:05.550
Let's sit here and think about it carefully.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:26.980
<b>Factoid: Cinnamoroll can actually flap his 
big ears and fly through the air.</b>

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.740
Kiki and Lala can fly too if they
have a star on their backs.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:31.750
I can't come up with anything.

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:33.280
Me, either.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.580
I kind of want a break.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.420
Our focus has certainly worn out.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.260
Maybe it is best to have a change of scenery.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.110
Training camp.

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:48.100
If you want to focus, have a training camp.

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:50.430
That might be a good idea!

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.030
Nice one, Shushu!

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:53.490
That might work.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:55.290
But where should we go?

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:56.090
Hawaii!

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:58.520
That'll take all our job money.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.000
Okinawa then.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.130
That's not too different.

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:03.780
Atami is fine then.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:06.260
That's not much of a compromise.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:09.250
I'd like to refrain from needless
spending as much as possible.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.790
What about a vacation home then?

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:16.230
Mom, how long have you been here?

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:19.040
One of our relatives has a
vacation home near the ocean.

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:22.300
Right, Seiichirou-san?

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.470
That place might definitely work.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.680
What do you guys think?

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.430
Let's go!

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.530
The ocean!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.560
Next Episode

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.690
Next time, "The Boys' Vacation".
